# The last page (plan/16 §5.3, replaced in plan/28 §6).
#
# It is `done` on disk and "Finish" in the sidebar: a plugin called `finished` would collide
# file-for-file with app-admin/calamares' own module. The two keys below are UPSTREAM'S, by
# upstream's names and with upstream's aliases, because the page changed hands and the
# configuration contract did not.
#
# `notifyOnFinished` is gone with the module that read it. It was false here and always had been —
# a D-Bus desktop notification about an installer that is the only application on the screen has
# no second window to be seen from — so the replacement does not implement it at all, which drops
# a QtDBus dependency and a code path nothing here exercised.
---
# The reboot checkbox is offered, unchecked. Unchecked deliberately: the user has to REMOVE THE
# INSTALL MEDIUM before rebooting, and a pre-ticked box invites them not to. The page says so, in
# a line that appears only once the box IS ticked.
#
# That instruction is not politeness. The installed root partition carries PARTLABEL=root_@VERSION@
# and the installed var carries PARTLABEL=var — identical to the labels on the stick this
# installer is running from, because those strings are the system's identity and are deliberately
# not profile-suffixed (plan/16 §3.4). With both disks attached, /dev/disk/by-partlabel/ resolves
# each name to whichever udev saw first, so the initrd's root=PARTLABEL=root_@VERSION@ and
# fstab's PARTLABEL=var can bind to either device. Booting with the stick still in is therefore
# ambiguous, and the ambiguity is per-partition — the live root with the installed /var is a real
# possible outcome, and it is the bad one.
restartNowMode:     user-unchecked
restartNowCommand:  "systemctl -i reboot"
